From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <datzeesix@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:54:36 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 56/95] Plutonium: the shells' tabs survive a restart

EXO-SESSION: PlutoniumTabSession writes every tab's address, tags and
opener kind to "Plutonium Tabs" in the profile (ImportantFileWriter, a
second after a change, never once shutdown has started) and opens them
again at the next start, once the startup shell's page exists. Incognito
tabs, DevTools and tabs of shells that reopen their own (T3 Code's) are
not saved.
